finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =168\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =139.278… \\\\  & ≈139{\\text{ in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =139-90 \\\\  & =49{\\text{ in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068aef71-9d0b-5bf0-a059-3345c4a26cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102411} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0ff031-ddc9-58a4-b121-fc07f61ea402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102412} {:answer/id #uuid "201fdfed-a087-5b36-9b41-dbae66a732df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102413} {:answer/id #uuid "28111f42-ee7e-5125-a586-64005136f60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102414} {:answer/id #uuid "77ca9711-f760-5ed4-9e2e-cc5dae5c27ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102415}] :answer-field/id #uuid "60055fce-3ff2-5b37-83d6-d6b9c5982646" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102410}] :question/id #uuid "76bfb6f5-5246-5d99-87f0-2edbbb96b1d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-18192" :question/problem "![](images/38/38004f5c93b047155973d32caa632c2c506d526c09ea891a7a02864997860f0e.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $15in^{2}$. What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d6fe5b-b93a-5b3a-b3ae-957d16951d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556429} {:answer/id #uuid "16b5e456-0628-5b28-9973-d24a67f59883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556479} {:answer/id #uuid "42dfb8fe-2ca7-5bf5-a862-8097a357954b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556578} {:answer/id #uuid "d645e81a-5337-5246-a811-91c0e07d93c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556952} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb5a129-5ab4-5d2c-9e01-2c562f075800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42dfb8fe-2ca7-5bf5-a862-8097a357954b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\text{ cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556578} :answer-field/id #uuid "04104815-55f0-5585-b546-93a2c497895f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e987c676-ae94-5f92-bdbb-ee11dc914f54" :question/math-academy-id "q-43310" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cce0e775722bbaaa8eeeb60a7cd097e8ad59b7c83c838f072416112aed657e33.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21}{4}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=3\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{21}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{21}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 3\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{21}{4} & =\\frac{3b}{4} \\\\ 3b & =21 \\\\ b & =7\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=7\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1135cf5-2a63-566c-bd0c-129c84f6e24a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104231} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e48878-b541-5b26-aae6-4283b0d479cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104232} {:answer/id #uuid "139637a3-5b2a-566b-8168-d2af651ada8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104233} {:answer/id #uuid "6b26f253-33e5-5837-ae42-4a92dbd57d87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104234} {:answer/id #uuid "75c57f27-6ce0-52e8-abe5-762ed4a75806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104235}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0cf5b5e1-1fb3-57b9-9af6-28ef54ceceb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3eb30020-a9be-5a7e-a00a-55c0ab165871" :question/math-academy-id "q-43343" :question/problem "![](images/19/192cd7673f9186480bd6ab9955e56eab78b8a4e3bbec9d8d824922b5fd9c0527.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{15\\sqrt{3}}{2}cm^{2}$. Determine $m∠A$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106439 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5668382-1e6c-5ada-8f6f-792ffd26ef91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104783} {:answer/id #uuid "e59316d1-4367-5461-a171-2a39cfa2466a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104784} {:answer/id #uuid "f212af3d-14ce-5430-8e0d-ebf2c473beac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104785} {:answer/id #uuid "358fdfcf-9dc7-5768-b6ee-2fbdf0a6a7b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "47.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104786} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7a3aa7-b0f9-5de4-b78a-8ca8b6f7052f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104787}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9e80d5c1-4641-5da9-a2bc-641c532e791f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104782}] :question/id #uuid "419a42dc-188f-5378-85e0-27d5bb64db37" :question/math-academy-id "q-54258" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cc23cf5b5df6c51aac404c9e6a95ba3cfbdb2279bcd3dea11c6d56966d91a8dd.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02e1a207-f9d0-53f3-b9be-3206f74c6704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512106} {:answer/id #uuid "992ff176-6fda-5a2c-8659-55baf90a83fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512458} {:answer/id #uuid "af6bec52-f2b1-55fa-890f-584e44e51b59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512510} {:answer/id #uuid "c3294de8-305e-5066-b9e4-7eebd339a6e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512565} {:answer/id #uuid "ea211255-4798-55dc-866b-aae486ca03e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "992ff176-6fda-5a2c-8659-55baf90a83fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512458} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5f55799-fa35-55be-b5e7-23ed06c306d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a33798d-52c0-57f6-a233-6585edd299f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-72754" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4ce20d9d732816efda0a2fd3aebabc467f9f2c73d0b6037f4ad8f95d8e8ef1e7.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/6e/6e070d26915bcb11118f5a23f36b80038d5dd865e32a8517a12c10939ca02f0b.png)\n\nFirst, we find the area of $△ABD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{85}^{∘} \\\\  & =24\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{85}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈23.908\\,7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area of $△BCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BCD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 14\\cdot 16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{36.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =112\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{36.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈66.462\\,9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BCD} \\\\  & ≈23.908\\,7+66.462\\,9 \\\\  & ≈90.371\\,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $90.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de0df21-0a88-5163-a683-4cb2c599085d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276166} {:answer/id #uuid "635eaa9c-9e71-5e09-a17f-e36fb0aaf504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276377} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2ac091-52e4-535b-ab71-86a951340114" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276739} {:answer/id #uuid "91235451-db3b-5880-8286-9c6007c9fb2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276792} {:answer/id #uuid "cad16388-db74-596b-823d-3c91bf52eae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad16388-db74-596b-823d-3c91bf52eae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277279} :answer-field/id #uuid "f80e5bf4-084f-512b-95c2-84b41e9a4184" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "56305129-86bb-5e37-8747-ef7193f88a5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161104" :question/problem "![](images/05/059cec995f7ef75b56b8c512af09051fe4631733e87d98d25065144500613f73.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $17{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{46}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 63\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{46}^{∘} \\\\  & =22.659… \\\\  & ≈23{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =23-17 \\\\  & =6{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2410c5d2-ad7f-56ab-b8c6-a7aad16f515d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275794} {:answer/id #uuid "3514b170-e1eb-53a5-9e81-17de317fd7f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275950} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb8bc3d-ff67-57f3-ae8b-552e2e72e1a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276333} {:answer/id #uuid "c02fcd5b-0741-5682-8bdc-226b818d2249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277183} {:answer/id #uuid "e8422d6a-5c26-57c8-91a3-e854994c2b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c02fcd5b-0741-5682-8bdc-226b818d2249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277183} :answer-field/id #uuid "54bd7b28-8ea6-5b14-9542-32ed882c403b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1a46e83d-b704-567c-8d00-1886b9f6bc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161107" :question/problem "![](images/ef/ef8379b21526455a723369fda4360e2d7d3ef3cf54ce7d7767df7bd160a169f4.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $5\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 5\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}\\,b}{4} \\\\ \\cancel{5\\sqrt{3}} & =\\frac{\\cancel{5\\sqrt{3}}\\,b}{4} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{b}{4} \\\\ b & =4\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=4\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a92871f-5bd5-581e-ac06-dbd13021c053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275724} {:answer/id #uuid "299f96e2-93fa-5d8f-ab41-fc313dbd3222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275854} {:answer/id #uuid "4f831c2c-96bc-514e-94a8-9c7ae9a2e9a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276188} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb62d91-e7c1-5a0b-9594-0da656f39663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276601} {:answer/id #uuid "a89eff61-0284-58bc-8453-86df1e739eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a92871f-5bd5-581e-ac06-dbd13021c053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275724} :answer-field/id #uuid "e821e218-a2a4-5efe-86d2-0f9a4556c28f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "43fd23a0-08b8-58ee-b7e6-43240cfa05d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161109" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b95571772af958b4f7b7dcdbba630b78e029c838340dc272809a6c7915dc9c90.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=6\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\,b}{2} \\\\ \\frac{21\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}}{\\cancel{2}} & =\\frac{3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}\\,b}{\\cancel{2}} \\\\ 3b & =21 \\\\ b & =7\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=7\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284783 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7be3af12-12f0-5cd1-bd3d-bc6bfd57dcfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282757} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e5da06-d9ea-53d3-908e-6037028c09ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49.76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283295} {:answer/id #uuid "bcbaee44-4ce0-5ebe-9ae5-2cef0ffbe0aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283325} {:answer/id #uuid "f1468e3f-6f85-57ba-8382-a6a2597ecc6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283792} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0ba284-2705-5fc9-9538-675c4f9b88c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "59.59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7be3af12-12f0-5cd1-bd3d-bc6bfd57dcfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282757} :answer-field/id #uuid "49f02eb2-409f-54e5-8bc0-c2750241a7a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a01c1b66-7a91-5db5-9419-74aedf0189de" :question/math-academy-id "q-18027" :question/problem "![](images/f1/f11e50891625fb39de472762aaaff23edf43372e37fcdf55d129da1125c0ff8a.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=26, \\\\ b & =AC=22, \\\\ m∠A & ={11}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘}=0.190\\,809,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 22\\cdot 26\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘} \\\\  & =286\\cdot (0.190\\,809) \\\\  & ≈54.57,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f78eeff4-6664-5afb-aa43-f6574f9a819d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f78eeff4-6664-5afb-aa43-f6574f9a819d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293897} :answer-field/id #uuid "52057c52-87e1-53a7-8ea5-eae346dfaaf1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "932a647f-64da-5961-9b0d-b120fe29bcc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-279752" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f41ad0635fb7bb426a387f825097a31dddb591861012f2543336a142832df9db.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ above is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=4, \\\\ a & =BC=8, \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}=0.642\\,788,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot (0.642\\,788) \\\\  & ≈10.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2e420a9-a7bd-5017-809e-98b732958447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2e420a9-a7bd-5017-809e-98b732958447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293632} :answer-field/id #uuid "d61c4e2c-bb73-58b5-9e0a-477efb52fb86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e614497f-203d-5c49-a415-3fb541b41cc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279753" :question/problem "![](images/68/68977537a5f180dd483534ed1415326251d4a76a3dd0833e9701487cd8b5b33d.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{ft}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=18, \\\\ b & =AC=12, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 18\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =108\\cdot (0.866\\,025…) \\\\  & ≈93.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6cee6b4-2a3f-5b80-8f79-bbdc774e729c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6cee6b4-2a3f-5b80-8f79-bbdc774e729c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293590} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0a67366-7358-5ccd-9b0a-b78d1e7fee7b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1e17900e-d26f-58a6-baab-ca3dab29afb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-279762" :question/problem "![](images/54/54265327c77bedb300fe0d1f1f08ca3ab2d7ae37f35f49007d3f20ab3a21dbaa.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/b1/b1d0cf7c5a7c6ad7f0f52c8686239920fabcb05be57372ae0c7c9c9491838a52.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈25.981,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 25.981 \\\\  & =51.962.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $52.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e971691-e630-503f-870f-b92b3ea2ce77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e971691-e630-503f-870f-b92b3ea2ce77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293443} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f6faf19-04cc-502f-9255-547f6f88a2b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8878e119-056d-550e-93df-4c14bd85326c" :question/math-academy-id "q-280260" :question/problem "![](images/20/200dcd87827ae9683ba0ecb3b284509b31d32f9e0dc1b9736a260d2f7d71b0a0.png)\n\nRounded to **two decimal places**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5, \\\\ a & =BC=5, \\\\ m∠B & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =12.5\\cdot (0.866\\,025) \\\\  & ≈10.83,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to **two decimal places**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bc3b7ba-d476-5a69-8384-cf1fc304c535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bc3b7ba-d476-5a69-8384-cf1fc304c535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293380} :answer-field/id #uuid "c798fd12-9751-5ada-a3f9-3336533400e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "95d92df8-f5a2-5d44-90e8-e2bcbdb9b2d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-280279" :question/problem "![](images/86/866f869f43e2663c2f63a485049f84ae059e2fdcb73db0445eb355491957c66a.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Then,  $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =5b\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 25\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} & =5b\\cdot \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\\\ 5b & =25 \\\\ b & =5\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=5\\,\\text{ cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc7bcb4a-1dc3-5347-9368-68572b9b7d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc7bcb4a-1dc3-5347-9368-68572b9b7d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293664} :answer-field/id #uuid "5521148e-fdbd-5362-a47a-ed6937115ac8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "13cfc4c2-60f9-5bce-a135-f2772aeb4d9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280282" :question/problem "![](images/5c/5c0bf3060129e2a03dab0fcd2a6f0f6068d1ec565143b83d11ad4d8ae1b41b85.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the acute triangle $△ABC$ is $3{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$ Then, the measure of $∠A$ is{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{ mm}, \\\\ b & =AC=4\\,\\text{mm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 3 & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45026583-2f3c-517d-8eb5-a28f4404f1e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45026583-2f3c-517d-8eb5-a28f4404f1e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295658} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0829f4e-98e2-572d-86bc-74f61d3d7503" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3bb44f47-acad-5cce-bb2a-a2f32b8da827" :question/math-academy-id "q-285703" :question/problem "![](images/da/dafaf2421aaa9be80c472b4dde7c941defb94f7f3533fda4ebb2fdcee2b60e31.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/cd/cd9363a3cc686ae45f49c982f4b31ad75b7c7897dcf7e8af58e530dba6946e1d.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & =21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈19.096\\,0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9+19.096\\,0 \\\\  & ≈35.182\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $35.2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d4ed0c9-7f6f-5206-af74-9b5a71b8bb26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d4ed0c9-7f6f-5206-af74-9b5a71b8bb26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295871} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa377d1-aa1d-58ff-8f43-f26275cc3530" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8934630b-77d1-55ee-b8d1-51a8be5db47e" :question/math-academy-id "q-285737" :question/problem "![](images/48/48dec69962b09e9c189de23c398db63066b6da8d62a04f1cd01fdc9f333f899f.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/d6/d6a654d3154ba8af8fc4f7654e62c6bacfede7017322aeed21a143e2634dcd14.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈13.856,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 13.856 \\\\  & =27.712.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $28.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f1e9b2-0fc8-53a9-bc65-f1cb3d45dfc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85f1e9b2-0fc8-53a9-bc65-f1cb3d45dfc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295985} :answer-field/id #uuid "16b8a569-d89d-5ee2-ba68-fe0246dbd470" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1777d556-717d-5159-9602-61018070f640" :question/math-academy-id "q-285740" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b69082ef86283bc842ce487b62901e8946ffff53ab8323a6fc846f68c5869aae.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $10{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{cm}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =11.591… \\\\  & ≈12{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "463216f3-e0fc-54f6-a6cb-048b38856ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "463216f3-e0fc-54f6-a6cb-048b38856ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295665} :answer-field/id #uuid "04e2c6a4-e805-5dc4-9dc9-998069258308" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "268ddd5a-7e79-59f1-bca0-b18bcf34aa98" :question/math-academy-id "q-285754" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d6923f5883ea770ce243eb23594740461a689c01f63de0421bc6f5d73a39531d.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $7{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =9.899… \\\\  & ≈10{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =10-7 \\\\  & =3{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbec2e0d-ab04-5eea-a9af-abd63ab0f708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbec2e0d-ab04-5eea-a9af-abd63ab0f708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296433} :answer-field/id #uuid "9353d69d-c96d-532a-a081-2fba2990886e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0087987a-958f-539c-9cad-7ab2dae7694f" :question/math-academy-id "q-285769" :question/problem "![](images/33/33aff6da54b72146f89bbd580a889a4050bff89bca86ddb6b74b80f62875a470.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $5{\\text{ km}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{km}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2.5\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =6.682… \\\\  & ≈7{\\text{ km}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =2{\\text{ km}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf942b6a-2bda-5195-bed6-c7db43c5e112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf942b6a-2bda-5195-bed6-c7db43c5e112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296279} :answer-field/id #uuid "dec8dded-fc4f-5c4b-9bb5-dd783b604c0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9ed8b4aa-f539-5288-91e4-4588aa44c54e" :question/math-academy-id "q-285786" :question/problem "![](images/af/aff2ca3dac212832eb3b2219678dab3f4029319ce6b09f8c134f9dcc99b72640.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $13{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 6.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16{\\text{ mi}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =16-13 \\\\  & =3{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2587a5f0-6774-56c5-ad31-19ae4ad1f0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2587a5f0-6774-56c5-ad31-19ae4ad1f0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321439} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7cc960-d17f-5d6a-bfe0-389ce724bbce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4332fa12-c2aa-5bc4-9e84-8c97ff265d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-365424" :question/problem "![](images/7e/7ead42d83a971733b601f45dcc1ad545a52298fc8a800ba69344651a54f4830d.png)\n\nThe area of the acute triangle $△ABC$ is $20\\sqrt{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Then, the measure of $∠A$ is{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=8\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=10\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =40\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{20\\sqrt{2}}{40} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00626454-06b5-5255-8b10-a969634f2a3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326940} {:answer/id #uuid "0a118cb1-bcf0-5192-ac99-50c6d218a0df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327022} {:answer/id #uuid "880cd774-4b0c-578b-9cb7-2a7f6ddc9ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328104} {:answer/id #uuid "9c24e516-7c4c-59ff-9120-8f3e8f967303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328284} {:answer/id #uuid "e1eb75a8-96e9-5751-9380-e070f3e6a153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "880cd774-4b0c-578b-9cb7-2a7f6ddc9ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328104} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cbb3be6-5963-5d28-9797-4fa8242fb4a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ffe80f4-577a-5763-8b79-42fa1192abfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-43328" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2a9f5e6149b62b5724de8a46e50e7aac2976ffa2f9f841c64417ffd248fcb88.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find the measure of $∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}} & =\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329721 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55cfe684-dc18-5ab1-b164-6d50fade618a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327676} {:answer/id #uuid "8d23ee9d-454e-5907-a98d-d759e11996ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328151} {:answer/id #uuid "b7359851-720e-5ab4-876a-6265d25f515d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328528} {:answer/id #uuid "cf531d87-8a79-5162-b024-e25dc07d7e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328757} {:answer/id #uuid "e7164a97-e526-5ef2-8ced-7e38b414e248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf531d87-8a79-5162-b024-e25dc07d7e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328757} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc9b871-5875-5e5c-8a91-d0aec6bf5882" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55d7cd50-6834-55b6-a52f-4f6d251b49dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-43339" :question/problem "![](images/85/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da74ef9-bc35-5bd4-a775-6227e3770b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330069} {:answer/id #uuid "4cab3170-0757-5382-a642-6a610aa18961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330646} {:answer/id #uuid "51dae920-7e93-5d91-8ef7-09f5119e363c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330692} {:answer/id #uuid "af914ae5-dadd-5a35-bda2-56290cd884a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331501} {:answer/id #uuid "e18ffbce-0f6c-59ce-84c9-1967feb16d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0da74ef9-bc35-5bd4-a775-6227e3770b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330069} :answer-field/id #uuid "489b8504-24f4-5803-ae22-0dec31049edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a963f45-1ffb-5d74-b38f-c635a0c24c20" :question/math-academy-id "q-54339" :question/problem "![](images/f1/f1ae263b71fa17fd648464c24b307c064c9e657c2c9f6b36faf8c9819f1fb285.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/a6/a60b049aef53aef28802b084b3e445fd6253978500ca981d3b799977523cdd71.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(8)(5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.383,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 16.383 \\\\  & =32.766.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $33.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03142fcd-6f19-5692-a3da-da502772ac2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333014} {:answer/id #uuid "0430ddd0-499d-53c2-994f-613bdc887648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333022} {:answer/id #uuid "454df806-b05f-5668-bfc1-d7cfdc549af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333630} {:answer/id #uuid "a5074c1a-1d5f-5090-b302-4eafa6e852a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334436} {:answer/id #uuid "d012d020-5f8d-544e-8a7f-5e3267236519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "69.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "454df806-b05f-5668-bfc1-d7cfdc549af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333630} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe2925de-ca80-5513-860d-a4f360e0060a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bbe5d0e1-3ef1-5eeb-b6da-bb45b64850c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-67787" :question/problem "![](images/48/488389632139d269e24958275ee20a9e5f8582fd0966e4d935487d238a463180.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/68/68f5708d49577befe9bac6a7aaf6a54fcdb30dcd344367d2c69b8924093dbb61.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 14\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & =84\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈56.315\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =17.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.994\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =56.315\\,8+16.994\\,8 \\\\  & =73.310\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $73.3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335940 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018db6be-c2e0-5b71-a965-9b8b09b6b735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "416" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333001} {:answer/id #uuid "0d660a41-028d-58ab-aa41-4492c238acc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "462" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333106} {:answer/id #uuid "30e73ae1-8ede-5d25-9355-5c9e2abec14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "458" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333440} {:answer/id #uuid "b829245a-508c-5df4-ab92-1586e59a733f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "437" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334602} {:answer/id #uuid "ec58f96d-7f07-5f65-a5c3-6ba3c108fcad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "422" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30e73ae1-8ede-5d25-9355-5c9e2abec14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "458" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333440} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fd4a639-ac17-50f3-9f71-1f9152848f0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dd32da9e-3e34-5cd6-ac25-c9a996a26523" :question/math-academy-id "q-67788" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0b100942a658966a5feea8a8677e7cfe86f21970a443385ff06034bbcb3d497.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ACD$ and $△ABC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/7e/7e3232258a523e4dbfebb6c380f5b88c2a54036b4d719e70ebf9060054f825d7.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ACD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 18\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =189\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈163.679,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△ABC:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 36\\cdot 30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘} \\\\  & =540\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈294.105,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ACD}+{A}_{ABC} \\\\  & =163.679+294.105 \\\\  & =457.784\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $458.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f07a6b5-32ea-529d-9160-238820145dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339267} {:answer/id #uuid "174b9032-2956-564a-826e-c2c81592003e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339336} {:answer/id #uuid "508acfdf-0761-5691-be12-cc8ecd53beb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339862} {:answer/id #uuid "84059e1d-50ea-57c1-a02c-e73cba67744f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340317} {:answer/id #uuid "f79db4a6-d5f5-5ae3-9697-f4ab3f3df76c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "508acfdf-0761-5691-be12-cc8ecd53beb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339862} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea1b3e9c-7be4-50dc-84b7-55a05c94254f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d86eb6a4-4303-50bf-b47a-fa898e3f8037" :question/math-academy-id "q-72764" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f53996727138b9442ac041cf492618db8287b54ba652c4f9e375cdde27dc1862.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{52}^{∘} \\\\  & =67.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{52}^{∘} \\\\  & =53.190… \\\\  & ≈53{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =53-34 \\\\  & =19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d011d15-855e-593b-a305-503c6f4d7b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339829} {:answer/id #uuid "5049855a-0cf1-52ff-a6d7-82ad580a1998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339858} {:answer/id #uuid "65970e9b-6b55-55f9-87cb-642a2bfcf59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "132" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340026} {:answer/id #uuid "810e57dc-6211-51e2-9530-7c30c274a5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340286} {:answer/id #uuid "941f7586-f901-520c-ba5a-d3f77fa4895c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5049855a-0cf1-52ff-a6d7-82ad580a1998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339858} :answer-field/id #uuid "59a7e60a-6a2a-50ed-b8ee-1ebc1c309e07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c1e965d5-3d0b-5c28-9671-3eb1e1598d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72768" :question/problem "![](images/36/36af7324fd2112d94feddc5a1a02a91d97bbc0866cb93a6ca711dd73f566305a.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/7c/7cfcb5cdf77b4afbf25afd64e37bb33f0ab2c211e09659181bfc16db0ccd2db7.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(18)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =72\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈67.658,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 67.658 \\\\  & =135.316.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $135.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b00af7-b5df-5196-b2de-1c4b578c6353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528150} {:answer/id #uuid "38ff0ae6-d364-5437-aee1-a57108c7d158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528156} {:answer/id #uuid "5e563a3e-30b4-58b1-9d8f-82d50ebca762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528168} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2e8905-558c-5e9d-bec6-bfbcdc9bbd18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528173} {:answer/id #uuid "9567582e-dc45-56ac-bc5f-3a111d30a323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e563a3e-30b4-58b1-9d8f-82d50ebca762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528168} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea4018e3-3df9-5608-859f-36d302fbcc24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "129248be-068c-5fed-a900-5e4f8d0a77cb" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f8a71c2cbb351253304bca516db5b4b7ca7ed745264083f9eb2bbdb918e19cc0.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The angles of a triangle sum to $180^{\\circ}$. Thus the included angle is\n\n$$\nm∠B=180^{\\circ}-73^{\\circ}-73^{\\circ}=34^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=9.28, \\\\ a & =BC=9.28, \\\\ m∠B & ={34}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{34}^{∘}=0.559\\,193,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9.28\\cdot 9.28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{34}^{∘} \\\\  & =43.0592\\cdot (0.559\\,193) \\\\  & ≈24.08,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e4b9075-c923-5501-aeee-25e2282c2b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.97" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528149} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5533f8-06f4-5369-b272-76225d4fe8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "371.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528159} {:answer/id #uuid "932d9fc0-5b73-50de-8465-aa7a923d7ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "371.10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528190} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c5dbc1-355d-5762-9187-a0ace7d2666b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "742.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528209} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e8f20a-1df1-524e-b4f2-26827cc6546e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "371.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8e8f20a-1df1-524e-b4f2-26827cc6546e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "371.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528215} :answer-field/id #uuid "4048902c-fcfa-5640-8cc3-acc24344e527" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3b677441-8745-5947-a9e5-2dd19f60b63a" :question/problem "![](images/45/4507bd5611cdf0324c470755c19274b04b9572b9c416e57b319aa444fce41e8b.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The angles of a triangle sum to $180^{\\circ}$. Thus the included angle is\n\n$$\nm∠B=180^{\\circ}-46^{\\circ}-46^{\\circ}=88^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=27.26, \\\\ a & =BC=27.26, \\\\ m∠B & ={88}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{88}^{∘}=0.999\\,391,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 27.26\\cdot 27.26\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{88}^{∘} \\\\  & =371.5538\\cdot (0.999\\,391) \\\\  & ≈371.33,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4254b5e-b4d4-56bc-bd8b-79e02ed7bf7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "921.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4254b5e-b4d4-56bc-bd8b-79e02ed7bf7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "921.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528220} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed27b396-d53a-5765-8d37-db0a89081e2e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528219}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4cab157d-9e84-52bf-83e6-fcd9af854df4" :question/problem "![](images/b4/b4d346c76ff55f7e183aefa579c49b54022e75ea4b723c5d74954c5257dcdf2f.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{ft}}^{2}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=50, \\\\ b & =AC=45, \\\\ m∠A & ={55}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘}=0.819\\,152,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 45\\cdot 50\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =1125\\cdot (0.819\\,152…) \\\\  & ≈921.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8c1d84-0382-586b-83cc-17222e776af1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "653.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528145} {:answer/id #uuid "99d1367c-8180-57c8-b14c-4ea0003f5f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "326.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528193} {:answer/id #uuid "9df5ad94-4cd1-54ce-9bea-b51a154b819a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22.86" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528194} {:answer/id #uuid "b87f6f9d-28fd-5dcd-9555-ca57c094855d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answe