=0.819\\,152,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 23.7\\cdot 29.9\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =354.315\\cdot (0.819\\,152) \\\\  & ≈290.24,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528213 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23377ec7-5f27-5dfb-a057-c056075f984f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78.46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528151} {:answer/id #uuid "29f22132-5f45-5aff-8a6f-2830b820b868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "321.73" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528153} {:answer/id #uuid "62557048-e863-5283-91cc-452739c28d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "178.98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528170} {:answer/id #uuid "712726a6-c8bf-5b90-ab00-ad839e5ec919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528176} {:answer/id #uuid "bff45295-0042-536f-9f71-52c399d6787d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144.59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "712726a6-c8bf-5b90-ab00-ad839e5ec919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528176} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d22e81c-e0f6-5195-bf6b-4b512a3851f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d47882fc-220e-59a2-aa68-6f709983b172" :question/problem "![](images/b5/b5ebff590d08903c465b3a5bb1359b6695f249ca61131332af899d0609f11ba8.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=22.8, \\\\ b & =AC=15.7, \\\\ m∠A & ={64}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{64}^{∘}=0.898\\,794,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15.7\\cdot 22.8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{64}^{∘} \\\\  & =178.98\\cdot (0.898\\,794) \\\\  & ≈160.87,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e911c7a-8b21-5d0a-b977-f82abae74339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "175.49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528175} {:answer/id #uuid "8391c6f4-1dc7-5770-8137-473f8afbd95d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528183} {:answer/id #uuid "a43cc271-0a01-510e-908a-081f05c4823e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "87.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528195} {:answer/id #uuid "b4db4353-6df7-5906-b949-73ea8aea923b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528203} {:answer/id #uuid "fb0bad98-2618-5617-a611-9579cc37f861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39.07" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a43cc271-0a01-510e-908a-081f05c4823e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "87.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528195} :answer-field/id #uuid "67b16069-92d7-5a91-99dc-58575a69406b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d89c8b9a-73d2-526f-bbef-c8af1e4be1d5" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c0740a227de0e72a080f8f323bb49b5d7ef0ac2f838217469f2e23c81049f628.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The angles of a triangle sum to $180^{\\circ}$. Thus the included angle is\n\n$$\nm∠B=180^{\\circ}-33^{\\circ}-33^{\\circ}=114^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=13.86, \\\\ a & =BC=13.86, \\\\ m∠B & ={114}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{114}^{∘}=0.913\\,545,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 13.86\\cdot 13.86\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{114}^{∘} \\\\  & =96.0498\\cdot (0.913\\,545) \\\\  & ≈87.75,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ee6c7b-5ed0-5fbc-bb1a-2eb180c50a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546468} {:answer/id #uuid "761357af-b1cf-58ba-aa81-8798f7d22c51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546514} {:answer/id #uuid "adee8728-bdb1-56dd-815f-113cd38c7423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546640} {:answer/id #uuid "e75bdd06-64ae-503e-b1d5-c6851246b93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546768} {:answer/id #uuid "f14b0185-0e87-545d-8523-8be2d0e389d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e75bdd06-64ae-503e-b1d5-c6851246b93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546768} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c4e9d14-c6c0-59b2-ad73-b4792a7449af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66cc8550-5653-59d7-83fc-1ba0962c771f" :question/math-academy-id "q-54340" :question/problem "![](images/87/873c7f6b6e036f592f693bf2d20e1980b890f888d08af40b775cb77deba07a76.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the parallelogram $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{BD}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ABD$ (see the illustration).\n\n![](images/75/7572dac85d8e6029b52d199bdfcb87b4a92ffafc008fe999c10848153f9f67d8.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ABD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{38}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{38}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈18.470,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ABD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 18.470 \\\\  & =36.940.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $37.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20078475-9fa7-56a0-a1a7-b2ef14a5f272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546320} {:answer/id #uuid "2288c623-2025-50ca-9e29-2593b12d6fac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "222" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546325} {:answer/id #uuid "c0de9861-7e04-5dd3-92eb-73257a63f700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "205" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546684} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf1bd15-fb6d-58ed-a02e-de5eab09e256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546708} {:answer/id #uuid "f4619caf-e3be-5779-a397-5eca1ee69630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "230" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4619caf-e3be-5779-a397-5eca1ee69630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "230" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546801} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b130ba-6ae3-550e-b29f-ba671825e730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "81669d7f-c6da-5c9d-8581-df25b358ada6" :question/math-academy-id "q-54338" :question/problem "![](images/24/243e5fd1911db6fc7dc940a16082c7369c63f913d78d9e18324d977540a310cb.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{BD}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△CBD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/da/da5c25d9e1e54a79b8e2c8532d4571dd42ccd4e6e6a3fa69aa1fc9075c19b39d.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△CBD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{CBD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(21)(12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & =126\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈115.107,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{CBD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 115.107 \\\\  & =230.214.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $230.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23429deb-9369-5516-be48-bb48841e8a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25.54\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546327} {:answer/id #uuid "42e3dabe-e7a8-51fe-a404-e5d96d282784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26.18\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546400} {:answer/id #uuid "62e52675-f9d0-5d2d-9fed-91450cd5dc88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27.28\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546466} {:answer/id #uuid "9998c88f-8e52-5ac6-9390-6df6fedb335a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25.13\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546591} {:answer/id #uuid "bb494bef-5e84-5f14-be2f-a36062cf1cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27.16\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62e52675-f9d0-5d2d-9fed-91450cd5dc88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27.28\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546466} :answer-field/id #uuid "8adb9f28-d5fd-5e0a-b9ed-5d8403d64ca3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bb68b570-72f8-5730-8942-1936207e20f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-67680" :question/problem "![](images/a8/a8cd5ca7760d21ac5bd86cfb90486ccde755f4aba831808889a20e1ad467eaf9.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ab\\operatorname{sin}⁡C,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠C$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =CA=8, \\\\ a & =CB=10, \\\\ m∠A & ={43}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}=0.681\\,998,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =40\\cdot (0.681\\,998) \\\\  & ≈27.28\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547053 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c48428d8-f9b3-5c4b-ae0e-754a6cffd216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "609" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c48428d8-f9b3-5c4b-ae0e-754a6cffd216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "609" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546690} :answer-field/id #uuid "42b88baf-cb77-56a0-9c63-111bcbcbb620" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cade1253-bc92-5811-80c5-a30e8af6f3ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-280272" :question/problem "![](images/9b/9b922282db5fce22af7df867b36545077f7d609dc83ef97abf46d5f9814cbc3c.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=36, \\\\ b & =AC=36, \\\\ m∠A & ={70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}=0.939\\,693,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 36\\cdot 36\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =648\\cdot (0.939\\,693) \\\\  & ≈609\\,{\\text{mi}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e986102-1442-5215-bb7a-26e13eca790a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546279} {:answer/id #uuid "3e950c3e-dd76-57ce-8d4e-431c7217bc82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546392} {:answer/id #uuid "67053cd1-8fc1-5bb6-ae87-cbe81bf6e79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546477} {:answer/id #uuid "7ffb8544-cee9-51c2-8e49-fb9eb933a279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546537} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1248f6-3036-5a4d-9f28-82ba65fe5f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e986102-1442-5215-bb7a-26e13eca790a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546279} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc7013e3-dd6c-5307-aa48-3cf975733d4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed23a91b-121e-53d9-8168-fa3e48b78557" :question/math-academy-id "q-67795" :question/problem "![](images/16/160b47689a56ef98c0a0d6b2df6dcf838857ba840ce017ac0707366304f68f83.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $112\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△BCD=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24\\cdot 16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =192\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =157.277… \\\\  & ≈157\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =157-112 \\\\  & =45\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ef5fd1-e6ce-548a-8813-a27dc903d97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "57\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546254} {:answer/id #uuid "237f7342-4d0b-5b9d-bfc6-b85c95c5663a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546328} {:answer/id #uuid "516f9d18-128b-53b7-9d34-ef5e89a5bf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546428} {:answer/id #uuid "54c332ef-cc47-5ca9-a704-d7e4834a6750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546436} {:answer/id #uuid "62663f15-c4d8-5ee2-b9af-d353992e1f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "69\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00ef5fd1-e6ce-548a-8813-a27dc903d97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "57\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546254} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6b15b1b-570c-54b0-b7d2-467ee5071f91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fe2449e6-7778-52c7-8e7c-b90034a289a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-67793" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca15b4523cd12bdfb4661624eba58387e15ebef6e228c1740b4582ba6af556a9.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $175{\\text{ in}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 27\\cdot 30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{35}^{∘} \\\\  & =405\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{35}^{∘} \\\\  & =232.298… \\\\  & ≈232{\\text{ in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =232-175 \\\\  & =57\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "091b27af-d7a1-515d-b104-eaa4d333ff68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556053} {:answer/id #uuid "112123cb-757e-592c-bcc5-657d79933f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "194.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556054} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf8c86f-5b8f-5088-b5b1-7fd64f54be93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "362.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556064} {:answer/id #uuid "e44db984-9187-5181-80fa-c663461bafab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556095} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3f1256-bf92-5f25-bf62-8b729543bd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "725.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf8c86f-5b8f-5088-b5b1-7fd64f54be93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "362.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556064} :answer-field/id #uuid "83ccab36-87a8-545e-a1f1-0e48f5eaae48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1fbc0c8f-18ed-5226-a1e4-557184738889" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b9343557caba8d0816ce08f755e124d1648780523145cd6864d3718550432014.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/59/59dd651e6e27665841463b1d6f8f8409801ca6bd5f15428e2cb5cf65328a2528.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 21.1\\cdot 22.1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =233.155\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈194.199\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24.2\\cdot 16.7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =202.07\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈168.308\\,4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈194.199\\,8+168.308\\,4 \\\\  & ≈362.508\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $362.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b48715f-d7f7-51ed-a8d7-39cfed0d2ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "138.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b48715f-d7f7-51ed-a8d7-39cfed0d2ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "138.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556067} :answer-field/id #uuid "717c1752-4a87-5be3-88ae-66ccafef2bf5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "52a9fe04-6346-5a39-ab8f-c86dd541521a" :question/problem "![](images/13/131fbdc1d3e47edd13257d415ee888c2148ccb3716bfd97ddaaa16efaa56db15.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/1f/1f848c8c4766a074b4c2b8e7ecc1e71d23e9c2c1c89158b8988ab36b53879f61.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 13.6\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{87.3}^{∘} \\\\  & =68\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{87.3}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈67.924\\,5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8.7\\cdot 19.9\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{54.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =86.565\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{54.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈70.736\\,1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈67.924\\,5+70.736\\,1 \\\\  & ≈138.660\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $138.7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b08d1199-8bf8-5b81-ba95-b6c22cf8c126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b08d1199-8bf8-5b81-ba95-b6c22cf8c126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556080} :answer-field/id #uuid "14440efa-6234-5e89-bd76-a3d48338cde5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "70e4dbc4-d39e-56c5-b732-6b1f3dd60ee8" :question/problem "![](images/44/44c617ba56886e7efe82d2b5624cb65effb54978ba810623990860d154830c40.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/44/44c617ba56886e7efe82d2b5624cb65effb54978ba810623990860d154830c40.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(6)(17)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =51\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈44.167,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 44.167 \\\\  & ≈88.334.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $88.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0087ce35-633e-5bb1-91c6-dc5054cd9772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556051} {:answer/id #uuid "224d4162-73d4-507d-9dff-d0df11cad464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556058} {:answer/id #uuid "582f4049-209c-5697-8586-2c2c755df426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "263.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556066} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf55c7a-7253-58e2-833b-d58e701c73f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556075} {:answer/id #uuid "df930634-6d70-5c54-97d3-326e30505e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "131.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df930634-6d70-5c54-97d3-326e30505e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "131.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556092} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe83946-b8fe-56a5-9860-fdb10eafbcb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9a106df8-a626-5ac9-9453-0adc6f724e4a" :question/problem "![](images/71/71a43ad32d3566fba8505542947532e9750a8d1289997b4f8f03e28ca313299f.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/89/8924aebb92b72747f67bc2e0c0a604dad541485a714bdcb1ee6da9f1c5f51310.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9.4\\cdot 27.1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{35.2}^{∘} \\\\  & =127.37\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{35.2}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈73.420\\,2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 13.9\\cdot 9.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{117.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =66.025\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{117.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈58.404\\,5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈73.420\\,2+58.404\\,5 \\\\  & ≈131.824\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $131.8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9e435db-0327-5a0d-89dd-6b6919442bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "94" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556078} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b5bed8-0df4-5779-a211-92c3cffb329c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "432" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556088} {:answer/id #uuid "c9707b78-0a7a-5dc5-a497-e949b9c08daa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556089} {:answer/id #uuid "df9eb1e0-6448-5054-97e0-b35a5285f814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "187" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556093} {:answer/id #uuid "fbdcecd0-ef54-5a3f-9109-c956203b15a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df9eb1e0-6448-5054-97e0-b35a5285f814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "187" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556093} :answer-field/id #uuid "240fe116-c60b-585d-bc29-6fabb08ceefe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a758c7b9-2fca-5f7b-9e41-1dd87720b0f0" :question/problem "![](images/67/67555c7ecb4ca726c4153c7b4e6bcd377f06534bb42cbdc5b696b697788847c4.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/67/67555c7ecb4ca726c4153c7b4e6bcd377f06534bb42cbdc5b696b697788847c4.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(18)(12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =108\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈93.531,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 93.531 \\\\  & ≈187.062.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $187.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79fffb65-226b-594a-aa22-0f4f4c72a6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556070} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d31c81-37cf-5e25-848b-3d24a03c8aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556084} {:answer/id #uuid "cdae530d-6cfa-5bc1-93ab-c4f4e2375cc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "252" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556090} {:answer/id #uuid "db6cc186-fe5e-57ed-a442-5decdd9bc1e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556091} {:answer/id #uuid "f7bcab47-0599-5d40-8019-94f89f8a64c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7bcab47-0599-5d40-8019-94f89f8a64c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556096} :answer-field/id #uuid "04b78953-d30d-5275-98b5-d8ee62cdd70f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b40fc366-4e09-5d72-87e3-127966410a40" :question/problem "![](images/58/589b9b43c038ffb4a4dafac8e8f42f936478230f3721e4386a4c0a061e62103b.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/58/589b9b43c038ffb4a4dafac8e8f42f936478230f3721e4386a4c0a061e62103b.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(14)(9)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =63\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈54.560,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 54.560 \\\\  & ≈109.120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $109.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556083 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28e03df9-8d32-5e16-97e1-d60734a64ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556060} {:answer/id #uuid "31d66741-51d6-54eb-a142-66b65661bc90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556061} {:answer/id #uuid "351a935e-7b5b-5e85-ab50-708f07e1c524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556062} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f19eed-e3b8-5f37-8f59-f52cd689c97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556081} {:answer/id #uuid "fc07f286-f460-598e-ab66-400dee68350b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31d66741-51d6-54eb-a142-66b65661bc90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556061} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa7c8b4-08f6-5285-b332-9a95f5c67461" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b411e2c1-d7e9-5814-9062-370425b62fa8" :question/problem "![](images/38/3844c3042ed7433f478f732aada7bfc73faa3f07608bf25778d4d87dc0a14968.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/38/3844c3042ed7433f478f732aada7bfc73faa3f07608bf25778d4d87dc0a14968.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(15)(5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =37.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈32.476,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 32.476 \\\\  & ≈64.952.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $65.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556085 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3709483f-4d15-50f4-9763-74ba51bf85fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3709483f-4d15-50f4-9763-74ba51bf85fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556063} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2be22cc-d519-5b67-bc44-6b6554e4d067" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bbc655be-2c25-5c4c-b0fb-845d3b2f8f24" :question/problem "![](images/24/245045911890f7cbd669087241954a3b100c6d15ec1bf511e4557d6e89c47db9.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The dashed diagonal divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/24/245045911890f7cbd669087241954a3b100c6d15ec1bf511e4557d6e89c47db9.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(11)(17)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =93.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈80.973,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 80.973 \\\\  & ≈161.946.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $162.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ac27400-1dfb-5d36-9cec-997cbda94fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ac27400-1dfb-5d36-9cec-997cbda94fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556074} :answer-field/id #uuid "941236ee-de88-5001-b113-1f06dfd6e21c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e0b03d8e-7815-590d-877d-b365e88392d9" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a941692b5253644845c4311baeb7d3e681a0c9091803440c5ecc0980494fbfc8.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/b4/b4b6aacce80889f8d867015f7f9c4400acba3d51fced00264062968c8295204a.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9.5\\cdot 10.3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120.7}^{∘} \\\\  & =48.925\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120.7}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈42.068\\,3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 13.4\\cdot 14.4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{76.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =96.48\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{76.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈93.774\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈42.068\\,3+93.774\\,8 \\\\  & ≈135.843\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $135.8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556097 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c641eab-ed7e-5b56-aa85-a6d95edb6429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "340.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c641eab-ed7e-5b56-aa85-a6d95edb6429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "340.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556056} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcfa3340-4566-58d3-8f9a-71cbe342dc62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fa65bbaf-475a-5c9e-a456-e1fba26eb1ce" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5a611645078047bb51f06d090a3be1b3628045067b106354fa62a167f7737c10.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point if needed.\n\nThe diagram is not drawn to scale. Use the marked measurements. The marked angles are rounded to the precision shown; calculate the area estimate using the marked values." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/cc/ccae61d17dd53252c3c08c885d92c7cc7444f97a339feed8db2e7568883e54ce.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 19.3\\cdot 18.7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{94.1}^{∘} \\\\  & =180.455\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{94.1}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈179.993\\,2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 11.6\\cdot 29.3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{71.2}^{∘} \\\\  & =169.94\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{71.2}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈160.873\\,6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈179.993\\,2+160.873\\,6 \\\\  & ≈340.866\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $340.9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049d033e-9ea7-58bc-bb55-6b11185d1b01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "049d033e-9ea7-58bc-bb55-6b11185d1b01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556352} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eaa9ff4-4551-5f33-ba72-289eaa72b4fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0921e1f0-6016-5a9a-b00a-281e162349d5" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa571435e7a44532cfb3bc61965b56b10e83c090236349851971e1b51c007ade.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{11}{2}\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ Use $\\sin30^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Then, $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=2\\text{ cm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{11}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{11}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{11}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{\\frac{11}{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\ b & =11\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=11\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff2e4436-f636-5aa3-88e5-00bf7a733fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff2e4436-f636-5aa3-88e5-00bf7a733fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556405} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce102e6e-9d86-54c9-b424-61ab30bebf30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1f90245f-9fc6-5863-a434-c42642a9ebf6" :question/problem "![](images/76/76bdcef8f267043fe1f9c97f989ff3d6bfdf3b071158501cf43aef78976e93eb.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64}\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ Then, $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\frac{43}{4}\\text{ cm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot \\frac{43}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot \\frac{43}{4}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64} & =\\frac{43\\sqrt{2}}{16}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{\\frac{1247\\sqrt{2}}{64}}{\\frac{43\\sqrt{2}}{16}} \\\\ b & =\\frac{29}{4}\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=\\frac{29}{4}\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b8b15ed-493d-56f0-91b4-96c0546ae3a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556362} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3aafe4-37fc-512f-9335-c0b5740cbecb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{7}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556375} {:answer/id #uuid "c2121115-e08d-5100-ac2e-6cef9261566c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556393} {:answer/id #uuid "e19dcdf1-d006-5161-a5fd-af6492cf1462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556398} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c66126-e596-580e-91de-79431398b6de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "294\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19dcdf1-d006-5161-a5fd-af6492cf1462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556398} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba9f84d4-40bc-5670-b78b-e2d89edb52b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "56e458c0-2e91-5258-b0ff-cd258f195c67" :question/problem "![](images/69/6949b198287b58d95ba47662a3432760d7e5a98d60bd006541269abcc9f3e2ab.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{mm}^{2}.$ Use $\\sin30^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=7\\text{ mm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{21}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{21}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 7\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{21}{2} & =\\frac{7}{4}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{\\frac{21}{2}}{\\frac{7}{4}} \\\\ b & =6\\text{ mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=6\\,\\text{mm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb0dc146-0b8f-5788-b4d6-1d2af2fc1489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb0dc146-0b8f-5788-b4d6-1d2af2fc1489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556404} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ea43d3b-18e5-535a-9041-c2927666f8ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "93b23a78-a854-5cfb-a02e-a33896d85d60" :question/problem "![](images/52/52e6b64e78550f0e1cfeecc59a606921b52af85c457fff5e936f45a0a732c243.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $1\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ Use $\\sin30^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Then, $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=2\\text{ cm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\ b & =2\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=2\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6f5fef-1f26-5927-9aba-3e07ba091909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "588\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556355} {:answer/id #uuid "1ddcbedc-9b6d-572c-a3ed-af91585959a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556358} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea08d46-2b55-577e-86f2-f830a33e8ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556382} {:answer/id #uuid "a5562289-9847-5a37-82e2-0f14fe73c7e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556385} {:answer/id #uuid "ba510cf0-a3a0-5d06-8f32-bab53002d3b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba510cf0-a3a0-5d06-8f32-bab53002d3b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556389} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ba1fed-347d-5277-b120-1a48f185cceb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604549