 :answer/value "\\frac{21}{8}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556395} {:answer/id #uuid "f893f514-4f5e-528a-8157-ca6cd7b413a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{63}{80}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d6abb05-37ef-5299-9ef6-0a9a17779c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556372} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba366e8a-53d8-5743-af27-e93d5394e3a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9f5682f6-556a-5e14-92ca-e2c5f602999e" :question/problem "![](images/89/89a4b38c29ef11835af24fa0b98ee45a7f5fcbc6ee0a5fd0a3de4d0096144659.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\frac{20}{3}\\text{ cm} \\\\ b & =AC \\\\ m∠A & ={135}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot \\frac{20}{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot \\frac{20}{3}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4} & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{3}b \\\\ b & =\\frac{\\frac{35\\sqrt{2}}{4}}{\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{3}} \\\\ b & =\\frac{21}{4}\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=\\frac{21}{4}\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17