h} :answer/value "42{\\text{ mi}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561429} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b00be6-a62a-5c2d-aa1b-2361ea2f66c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "246{\\text{ mi}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561439} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2094fc-e122-54c3-af59-c5401f10502e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93{\\text{ mi}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98680abc-438b-5a01-9298-1169053f5980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42{\\text{ mi}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561429} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b04ea8d-6fd7-5257-94b3-53ca685f87b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6f48ce8b-cecb-533a-9b78-d507db11175a" :question/problem "![](images/5c/5c90b8329b7c163cf4aff55af1bd45d21bc8487fcbf39c4b7b625b31d19bbb57.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $102{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.$ What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 18\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 288\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\ & ≈144{\\text{ mi}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\ & =144-102 \\\\ & =42{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1458115d-10e6-5e7e-b0fe-8e29ca308733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "71{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561388} {:answer/id #uuid "2db67ade-cdab-58dd-8159-2a40d0681526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561399} {:answer/id #uuid "2de89c29-484f-51e3-a5ef-80b0ed2cef3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561400} {:answer/id #uuid "b87d47b3-2cae-59e7-860c-28f55693fdd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561434} {:answer/id #uuid "ddab5931-9566-53a6-a72e-6b1a6edad62c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2de89c29-484f-51e3-a5ef-80b0ed2cef3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561400} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b4a1f4a-e30c-5d9a-8739-b2a26e495f6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "95b7234e-7744-581a-a282-09577ca5a31a" :question/problem "![](images/13/13ec62338798667cc6d164a32cb8dd4c0f6596eb7c3a6e0519cc492e80225877.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $25{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$ What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 96\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\ & ≈48{\\text{ mm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\ & =48-25 \\\\ & =23{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561437 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13fa3949-89d4-57d3-8cdf-16c0eb40ce6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561387} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7768f2-6413-5fae-8725-57c4bedccb07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561398} {:answer/id #uuid "3124f5e6-c509-56b8-8bc7-055ff972b970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "99{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561403} {:answer/id #uuid "856cc125-2c58-5183-80aa-e2a37b30b90c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561423} {:answer/id #uuid "9c594856-7359-580f-ba95-301b91c5962e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "141{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13fa3949-89d4-57d3-8cdf-16c0eb40ce6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{\\text{ mm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561387} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f95e495-8770-5e1c-a1e5-a190f92c7426" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bf54d5bd-b74b-5410-8f38-b48a5069f40d" :question/problem "![](images/06/06d308a50c664795dd52ae3be40da7a0c23882fb11ba1d0f8f5d9d29bf1331a1.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $61{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$ What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 160\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\ & ≈80{\\text{ mm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\ & =80-61 \\\\ & =19{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186586574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19de51f5-eeb7-5c11-8927-b90ba968537a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585929} {:answer/id #uuid "361501ed-2bb7-5905-933e-93a1a009669b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "102.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585986} {:answer/id #uuid "a4a56e30-9a91-5bd1-a3e8-41a8310f5c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186586215} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4df6c9-3005-5b8b-bab2-9bad01afd4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186586255} {:answer/id #uuid "c95dedbb-7121-506c-971b-b96d65875737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186586275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4a56e30-9a91-5bd1-a3e8-41a8310f5c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186586215} :answer-field/id #uuid "deb86f76-a793-58a4-8b02-9be83c273afb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186586507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7fff9862-4765-59f3-b9bb-3fdc75b8af45" :question/math-academy-id "q-72756" :question/problem "![](images/72/721f8231c38ba5937b4e2f80233f83ecb52605388897291d14968064f214a4c4.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/2b/2bdf5043e8bd25884eeda042c276fad2e5fa267e1f9f19d9271564576965d09a.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{110}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{110}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈28.190\\,7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 13\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{58}^{∘} \\\\  & =97.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{58}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈82.684\\,7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =28.190\\,7+82.684\\,7 \\\\  & =110.875\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $110.9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4daa482a-db01-5201-9c69-f47ee45ebded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4daa482a-db01-5201-9c69-f47ee45ebded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603426} :answer-field/id #uuid "b74ffb2c-f1b2-50df-a175-8e2324b55e0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "243aa0c3-2135-51ae-adaf-9651412ecad8" :question/math-academy-id "q-280276" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5f9574fad2615ba517ed8486ab7c054b53f25184617a345afb76fca78ab9b224.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $24\\sqrt{3}{\\text{ in}}^{2}.$ Then, $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{in}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=8\\text{ in}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 24\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\ 24\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 8\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\ 24\\sqrt{3} & =2\\sqrt{3}b \\\\ 24\\cancel{\\sqrt{3}} & =2\\cancel{\\sqrt{3}}b \\\\ 2b & =24 \\\\ b & =12\\text{ in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=12\\text{ in}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c70c067-2fbe-5805-abf9-82d9cbb72f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c70c067-2fbe-5805-abf9-82d9cbb72f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603284} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c177f16-01e3-503a-87e9-c718be9d775b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "34b679af-faa1-5c8b-93bc-eb57572e813a" :question/math-academy-id "q-271477" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d691321f765094f492ec72076e96e13af0016f7b692cceba5f8d6aab21180f65.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{15\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Then,  $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{15\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{15\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}\\,b}{2} \\\\ \\frac{15\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}}{\\cancel{2}} & =\\frac{5\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}\\,b}{\\cancel{2}} \\\\ 5b & =15 \\\\ b & =3\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=3\\,\\text{ cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2af98c39-ac41-5848-b287-39f4f0b5086f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "67\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603347} {:answer/id #uuid "384d8634-82f9-5e0e-8b1a-e451e1ba0ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "86\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603383} {:answer/id #uuid "7aae468a-1023-5b4a-a043-2053099316d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603523} {:answer/id #uuid "7d9de1ef-56e4-58ed-93f0-17479eb19385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603532} {:answer/id #uuid "a470d8a2-15f9-5d5e-b2dc-93b7676f36d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aae468a-1023-5b4a-a043-2053099316d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603523} :answer-field/id #uuid "94bcfd98-ea17-55ba-a90d-de6d096c5ff6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186603922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bfe01a47-0bae-5ba1-bce0-856215b36fe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-67794" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cc376c3193693561bb65a6296fe8fb798f36f1b5f1152aba46c14a443887702c.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $130\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24\\cdot 18\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{115}^{∘} \\\\  & =216\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{115}^{∘} \\\\  & =195.762… \\\\  & ≈196\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =196-130 \\\\  & =66\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3489db86-0989-5652-a751-63344e0ad6b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46.72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719110} {:answer/id #uuid "4951ec10-f9ad-575a-985c-e806d92cc796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719111} {:answer/id #uuid "59d51095-58f0-50b7-b235-a23833bc1c51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719113} {:answer/id #uuid "6be1ad2c-8441-5762-b123-0a0574f25724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70.41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719116} {:answer/id #uuid "b1fc7d53-10d6-5979-82a8-e018a295397b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59d51095-58f0-50b7-b235-a23833bc1c51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719113} :answer-field/id #uuid "fee47a1a-046a-52db-9c7e-9d49b6c6fbc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "523e58fd-720f-5d57-874d-652c697b8c8b" :question/problem "![](images/77/77419eacd4ad3c33252b635ad4763ab21c5a2c9072b18f098340efead5a1e12e.png)\n\nFind the area of $\\triangle ABC$, in square units. Round your answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n> Use a scientific calculator in degree mode." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The sides $CA=9$ and $CB=13$ meet at $C$, so $37^{\\circ}$ is their included angle. Use\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A=\\frac12(CA)(CB)\\sin C.\n$$\n\nSubstituting gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A&=\\frac12(9)(13)\\sin 37^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=58.5\\sin 37^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=35.20617885\\ldots\\\\\n&\\approx35.21.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area is $35.21$ square units. Keep the calculator's full precision until the final rounding."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ceaaee1-4c4e-51d3-9314-362100c1bd6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719117} {:answer/id #uuid "27755c8d-7624-493a-b856-24e85cbc863a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ceaaee1-4c4e-51d3-9314-362100c1bd6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719117} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf83c12-ad93-5430-abe6-66c8461ab17b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719121}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "62053f65-aa41-51ba-ae55-9daf395476d3" :question/problem "![](images/9f/9f5c8eff55cd477831f43d3d8508ca76c4f428dba474c1f68b84ff76b571ff10.png)\n\n$E$ lies on $BC$. The two marked angles at $A$ are $\\angle BAE=24^{\\circ}$ and $\\angle EAC=30^{\\circ}$.\n\nRounded to **two decimal places**, the area of $\\triangle ABC$ is {{field-1}} square units.\n\n> Use a scientific calculator in degree mode." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The included angle between $AB=8$ and $AC=11$ is the whole angle $\\angle BAC$, not either marked part. Add the adjacent angles:\n\n$$\n\\angle BAC=24^{\\circ}+30^{\\circ}=54^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nUse these two sides and their included angle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A&=\\frac12(AB)(AC)\\sin(\\angle BAC)\\\\\n&=\\frac12(8)(11)\\sin54^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=44\\sin54^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=35.59674775\\ldots\\\\\n&\\approx35.60.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area is $35.60$ square units. Using only $24^{\\circ}$ or $30^{\\circ}$ with sides $AB$ and $AC$ would pair those sides with the wrong angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae06f8fe-d083-5d57-8c42-30226a15d1a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58.41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae06f8fe-d083-5d57-8c42-30226a15d1a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58.41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719119} :answer-field/id #uuid "664e0772-c077-5c42-b3a4-2b9c4dfd1901" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9f6e2d93-8e5c-5502-80c2-43af157cdfdc" :question/problem "![](images/6c/6caafe3e5db48af9acf0fe404d10eadc112fb1b9dc4e3b9a62aafad234b7fef2.png)\n\n$E$ lies on $AB$. The two marked angles at $C$ are $\\angle BCE=28^{\\circ}$ and $\\angle ECA=40^{\\circ}$. The side lengths are $CA=x+2$ and $CB=2x$, and $CA+CB=23$. All lengths use the same unit.\n\nRounded to **two decimal places**, the area of $\\triangle ABC$ is {{field-1}} square units.\n\n> Use a scientific calculator in degree mode." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First determine the two side lengths. Their sum is $23$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x+2)+2x&=23\\\\\n3x+2&=23\\\\\nx&=7.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $CA=x+2=9$ and $CB=2x=14$.\n\nThe included angle between these sides is the whole angle $\\angle ACB$. Add its two marked parts:\n\n$$\n\\angle ACB=28^{\\circ}+40^{\\circ}=68^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nNow apply the triangle area formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A&=\\frac12(CA)(CB)\\sin(\\angle ACB)\\\\\n&=\\frac12(9)(14)\\sin68^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=63\\sin68^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=58.41258283\\ldots\\\\\n&\\approx58.41.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area is $58.41$ square units. Use the side lengths $9$ and $14$, rather than $x$ itself. Both the side expressions and the two angle markings must be combined before substituting into the formula."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b698e57-7d53-5474-9782-97e04b05c155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719347} {:answer/id #uuid "5268720e-5db0-51d1-bd1e-f5643213f842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719348} {:answer/id #uuid "9d2a0ca7-5e3b-5c24-a515-d8fe89ce5220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719352} {:answer/id #uuid "c15aca46-80f8-5cf3-8d6c-e490aec30bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719354} {:answer/id #uuid "e8156611-b5ad-5571-95e8-2b1e7d3132d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8156611-b5ad-5571-95e8-2b1e7d3132d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719356} :answer-field/id #uuid "868ac817-add1-5c22-8b6e-6cad3f3ba3b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "032fd9c9-6030-5233-86b9-d9d0cc5e552d" :question/problem "![Triangle ABC with the given side lengths and included angle](images/d4/d44a2489624bbf83404fd0d663e57d9cf60fe107148ce3672c8e0f85fdd91bb4.png)\n\nThe area of $\\triangle ABC$ is $12\\,\\text{cm}^2$. Find $AC$.\n\nUse $\\mathcal A=\\frac12(AB)(AC)\\sin A$ and $\\sin 30^\\circ=\\frac12$.\n" :question/worked-solution "The angle at $A$ is between $AB$ and $AC$. Let $x$ be the length of $AC$ in centimeters. Substitute the area, $AB=6$, and the supplied sine value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12 &= \\frac12\\cdot 6\\cdot x\\cdot\\frac12 \\\\\n12 &= \\frac32 x \\\\\nx &= 12\\cdot\\frac23=8.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $AC=8\\,\\text{cm}$. Checking gives $\\frac12\\cdot6\\cdot8\\cdot\\frac12=12\\,\\text{cm}^2$.\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d799dda3-4d1f-521b-88ef-bd960504c509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d799dda3-4d1f-521b-88ef-bd960504c509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719355} :answer-field/id #uuid "08ae6e74-a5b8-5c50-8207-90476ffeb90b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5e15568a-ae30-5c44-8ec8-7185a693c4f6" :question/problem "![Triangle ABC with the given side lengths and included angle](images/af/af267754b67b2b9485f81406d3b104941c2b543f885a4a39729a8dfe12dcbdf6.png)\n\nThe area of $\\triangle ABC$ is $12\\,\\text{cm}^2$. The angle $A$ is obtuse. Find its exact measure.\n\n$m\\angle A=$ {{field-1}} $^\\circ$.\n" :question/worked-solution "The known sides $AB=4\\sqrt2\\,\\text{cm}$ and $AC=6\\,\\text{cm}$ meet at $A$. Apply the area formula and isolate the sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A &= \\frac12(AB)(AC)\\sin A \\\\\n12 &= \\frac12\\cdot4\\sqrt2\\cdot6\\sin A \\\\\n12 &= 12\\sqrt2\\sin A \\\\\n\\sin A &= \\frac1{\\sqrt2}=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWithin a triangle, both $45^\\circ$ and $135^\\circ=180^\\circ-45^\\circ$ have this sine. Since $A$ is obtuse, choose $135^\\circ$.\n\nTherefore, $m\\angle A=135^\\circ$. Checking the area gives $\\frac12\\cdot4\\sqrt2\\cdot6\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}=12\\,\\text{cm}^2$.\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "384d4093-030b-5659-b224-f7430bc26838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "384d4093-030b-5659-b224-f7430bc26838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719346} :answer-field/id #uuid "7417558f-55cb-5cb7-b977-8de7fdef093a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bb9d50af-2620-5929-aa11-44d96c90502b" :question/problem "![Triangle ABC with the given side lengths and included angle](images/a9/a93948e32049d3dd2554108aa8be39aee76ee34cd754c41d7967d86c05040af2.png)\n\nThe area of $\\triangle ABC$ is $15\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}^2$. Find $AC$.\n\n$AC=$ {{field-1}} $\\text{cm}$.\n" :question/worked-solution "The $60^\\circ$ angle is included between $AB=10\\,\\text{cm}$ and the unknown side $AC$. Let $x$ be the length of $AC$ in centimeters. Use $\\mathcal A=\\frac12(AB)(AC)\\sin A$ and recall that $\\sin 60^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n15\\sqrt3 &= \\frac12\\cdot10\\cdot x\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2} \\\\\n15\\sqrt3 &= \\frac{5\\sqrt3}{2}x \\\\\n15 &= \\frac52 x \\\\\nx &= 6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $AC=6\\,\\text{cm}$. Substitution gives $\\frac12\\cdot10\\cdot6\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}=15\\sqrt3\\,\\text{cm}^2$.\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991c14ae-6eed-5d12-bc92-8c99e9e186ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "991c14ae-6eed-5d12-bc92-8c99e9e186ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719426} :answer-field/id #uuid "798d26d7-a43f-5780-a9fa-2dde20394e1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3880915b-be34-5e93-9a2a-e3d1ea50d81c" :question/problem "The dashed diagonal $BD$ divides parallelogram $ABCD$ into two congruent triangles. Find the area of the parallelogram, rounded to the nearest tenth.\n\n![](images/ea/ea69a710d57a04c208486f77f7d979a97910ce347090076f449c8c15896d2076.png)\n\nFor a triangle, use $A=\\frac12 ab\\sin C$, where $C$ is the angle between sides $a$ and $b$. Find the area of $\\triangle ABD$, then double it.\n\nArea: {{field-1}} square units.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point. A scientific calculator in degree mode may be used." :question/worked-solution "The sides $AB=9$ and $AD=7$ enclose the $50^\\circ$ angle in $\\triangle ABD$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABD}&=\\frac12(9)(7)\\sin50^\\circ\\\\\n&=31.5\\sin50^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx24.1304.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two triangles are congruent, so the parallelogram has twice this area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD}&=2A_{ABD}\\\\\n&=63\\sin50^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx48.2608.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeeping full calculator precision until the final rounding gives $\\boxed{48.3}$ square units."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719418 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b36a868-82fe-52ae-ac04-bca55e3e2cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719417} {:answer/id #uuid "56c6b541-1db6-5121-b966-86cace9dedcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719419} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4e6802-c990-5139-87b7-e9cf9189ee1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719420} {:answer/id #uuid "64cd029f-6391-582f-8b4f-f802cdc9c661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719422} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf32b81-3cfa-5a93-be8b-7d2bc3a330db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbf32b81-3cfa-5a93-be8b-7d2bc3a330db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719428} :answer-field/id #uuid "b33d2303-1060-5c8a-822f-d628caf54794" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "528253e6-fd58-5078-972a-f04f9bf8adcb" :question/problem "Find the area of quadrilateral $ABCD$, rounded to the nearest tenth. All side lengths are in units.\n\n![](images/37/37a061b85d2c848277c6307356d0f0c8411060146c898d3f906037a381c2b9a1.png)\n\nA scientific calculator in degree mode may be used." :question/worked-solution "Draw diagonal $BD$. It splits the quadrilateral into $\\triangle ABD$ and $\\triangle BCD$, whose areas must be added.\n\n![](images/cc/cc69a1e3b37e7d77be2b39122dbf17c20daa86a8fe7c6d8578f9fd55dcb83f90.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABD$, the $60^\\circ$ angle is between the sides of lengths $8$ and $12$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABD}&=\\frac12(8)(12)\\sin60^\\circ\\\\\n&=48\\sin60^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx41.5692.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $\\triangle BCD$, the $120^\\circ$ angle is between the sides of lengths $4$ and $8$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{BCD}&=\\frac12(4)(8)\\sin120^\\circ\\\\\n&=16\\sin120^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx13.8564.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the areas, retaining full calculator precision:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD}&=A_{ABD}+A_{BCD}\\\\\n&=48\\sin60^\\circ+16\\sin120^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx55.4256.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo the nearest tenth, the area is $\\boxed{55.4}$ square units. Doubling either triangle's area would be incorrect: these two triangles are not congruent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "888fe14b-fc61-5309-a656-11decb8d8d25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "888fe14b-fc61-5309-a656-11decb8d8d25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719424} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ed22735-8371-525e-b402-1d4507c97a30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5d69175d-75c5-51fe-9a2e-64b83bba6f76" :question/problem "In convex quadrilateral $ABCD$, $AB=10$, $AD=8$, and the diagonal $AC=12$. The full angle $\\angle DAB=110^\\circ$ and $\\angle BAC=35^\\circ$.\n\n![](images/05/05dfe4b721ff22ac11aa4e3319d0cb4caa144cb209a4f812aa30c6b6e034f8a3.png)\n\nFind the area of $ABCD$, rounded to the nearest tenth.\n\nArea: {{field-1}} square units.\n\nEnter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point. A scientific calculator in degree mode may be used." :question/worked-solution "Diagonal $AC$ lies inside the convex quadrilateral and splits the full angle at $A$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\angle CAD=110^\\circ-35^\\circ=75^\\circ.\n$$\n\n![](images/7c/7c7c4df1668bad7dde4f65e0ed7af6f54fc6f5c0d435bf6f3539c274d8321f66.png)\n\nUse the shared side $AC=12$ in both triangles. The included angle for the sides $AB$ and $AC$ is $35^\\circ$, whereas the included angle for $AC$ and $AD$ is $75^\\circ$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABC}&=\\frac12(10)(12)\\sin35^\\circ\\\\\n&=60\\sin35^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx34.4146,\\\\[4pt]\nA_{ACD}&=\\frac12(12)(8)\\sin75^\\circ\\\\\n&=48\\sin75^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx46.3644.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangles occupy the whole quadrilateral without overlapping, so add their areas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD}&=A_{ABC}+A_{ACD}\\\\\n&=60\\sin35^\\circ+48\\sin75^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx80.7790.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound only the final total: $\\boxed{80.8}$ square units. The full $110^\\circ$ angle is not an included angle of either triangle in this decomposition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0e4480-3f9f-5741-97af-f4b8294aea08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719514} {:answer/id #uuid "4b6f59c3-3053-5bd6-b242-2ba4c69ec606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719517} {:answer/id #uuid "5c53681c-bdc6-59df-9ce3-30605d44d37c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719518} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8d753c-d120-522a-8eb9-e100bf007209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719524} {:answer/id #uuid "e1519887-bffc-577a-8b98-a1b34912c293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1519887-bffc-577a-8b98-a1b34912c293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719528} :answer-field/id #uuid "916f9d49-87cf-506b-bf7a-fe70c31e1066" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "131b6086-c5f6-5a45-ba15-3a463928baae" :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral ABCD with dashed segment BD](images/0a/0a75121a020299d669f3dff640880bd837dd270911c60e955063b04b85e57018.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $28\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ The enclosing triangle $ABD$ has area $40\\,\\text{cm}^{2}$. What is the area of $\\triangle BCD$?" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The dashed segment $BD$ completes the enclosing triangle $ABD$. Its area is the sum of the areas of the quadrilateral and the missing triangle:\n\n$$\nA_{ABD}=A_{ABCD}+A_{BCD}.\n$$\n\nSubtract the quadrilateral's area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{BCD}&=A_{ABD}-A_{ABCD}\\\\\n&=40-28\\\\\n&=12\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da518a16-2c76-596b-aeb0-34686439cbf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da518a16-2c76-596b-aeb0-34686439cbf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719527} :answer-field/id #uuid "61f682c4-27e5-5d32-81f2-0fc1b12fca25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4ac15706-aef3-5c80-b90d-2209100282bf" :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral ABCD with dashed segment BD](images/87/872338605084c225802cf1e5b7069938fb5d6f61b9cbe85312d28ecc2baf8852.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $32\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ The area of $\\triangle BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is {{field-1}} $\\text{cm}^{2}$.\n\nA scientific calculator is required." :question/requires-calculator true :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "The known sides $AB=12\\,\\text{cm}$ and $AD=9\\,\\text{cm}$ meet at the included angle $112^\\circ$. Use the sine-area formula for the enclosing triangle $ABD$, with the calculator in degree mode:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABD}&=\\frac12\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot\\sin\\angle BAD\\\\\n&=\\frac12\\cdot12\\cdot9\\cdot\\sin112^\\circ\\\\\n&=54\\sin112^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx50.067928\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $BCD$ is the part of $ABD$ outside the quadrilateral. Subtract before rounding, keeping the calculator's full precision:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{BCD}&=A_{ABD}-A_{ABCD}\\\\\n&=54\\sin112^\\circ-32\\\\\n&\\approx18.067928\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, its area is $18\\,\\text{cm}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719520 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c96ebf8-880e-5014-8685-1dde605246ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719512} {:answer/id #uuid "489e3e02-8c3b-5fec-98db-fb8c7608259e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "79\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719515} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5022b2-c586-5ea3-8288-1a6ca1525ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719522} {:answer/id #uuid "a54f1286-ddf8-526d-980c-ae1130b4c990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719523} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cfed16-2277-51dd-bd30-b42a4cb7ced2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c5022b2-c586-5ea3-8288-1a6ca1525ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719522} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7ee2991-7cef-5d39-90f1-7605b948cf99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6c2c49f6-fe97-57c7-b103-30957bc434c9" :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral ABCD with dashed segment BD](images/45/452345c7dbf36abe26d85eb4cfaadd88b48e5dc91b12027d491be12101e98670.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $31\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.$ The angle at $A$ is a right angle. What is the area of $\\triangle BCD$?" :question/worked-solution "First find the area of the enclosing triangle $ABD$. Since $AB$ and $AD$ are perpendicular, they are its base and height:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABD}&=\\frac12\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\\\\n&=\\frac12\\cdot8\\cdot12\\\\\n&=48\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral and the missing triangle $BCD$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{BCD}&=A_{ABD}-A_{ABCD}\\\\\n&=48-31\\\\\n&=17\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719587 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88062318-2078-50bb-98f8-80a767930105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34.48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719595} {:answer/id #uuid "9820cb8c-9155-5f17-9df8-8869978d4fd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719596} {:answer/id #uuid "a01757aa-7330-517a-ab99-462f075c0461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45.59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719598} {:answer/id #uuid "a45990f3-89a9-500e-952f-5e3a8ae0882a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719599} {:answer/id #uuid "c53c15f5-016e-58ec-9bde-c75084e85beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a45990f3-89a9-500e-952f-5e3a8ae0882a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719599} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c9f329-661f-50f6-8ba6-72336391f086" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "213392a5-2184-5c13-b83b-580d9e343fab" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0b5deef545caf2423c2d146a66c7668a7e78a9eb3d8fcb77426a8369adcf85d0.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABC$, $AC=8$ and $AB=14$. The included angle is $\\angle CAB=109^{\\circ}$.\n\nFind the area of $\\triangle ABC$, in square units. Round your answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n> Use a scientific calculator in degree mode." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The sides $AC=8$ and $AB=14$ meet at $A$, so $109^{\\circ}$ is their included angle.\n\nApply the triangle area formula to those two sides and their included angle.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A&=\\frac12(AC)(AB)\\sin(\\angle CAB)\\\\\n&=\\frac12(8)(14)\\sin 109^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=56\\sin 109^{\\circ}\\\\\n&\\approx 52.94904023\\\\\n&\\approx 52.95.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area is $52.95$ square units. Keep full calculator precision until the final rounding."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719588 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0d5214-411b-53df-b354-c63660aeff70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719584} {:answer/id #uuid "1707c4ab-4b52-5468-9809-aba069d97e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719585} {:answer/id #uuid "7eaff3c7-c7a1-5cdf-b105-24e67b5d5a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719594} {:answer/id #uuid "9c979102-80a6-5fff-84c3-32752e8a891f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "74.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719597} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c2a30c-5b79-5382-b475-8e5635dc0463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "106.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1707c4ab-4b52-5468-9809-aba069d97e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719585} :answer-field/id #uuid "7576ba82-f4b4-5091-99cb-aec55e160785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "40a3bb37-1933-5bf7-9714-8ccbad67a7c1" :question/problem "![](images/66/665061a3ef5b9857509707bb3833ad70ab7ec4f80acc828ec6706193608551a6.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABC$, $CB=10$ and $CA=16$. The included angle is $\\angle BCA=56^{\\circ}$.\n\nFind the area of $\\triangle ABC$, in square units. Round your answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n> Use a scientific calculator in degree mode." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The sides $CB=10$ and $CA=16$ meet at $C$, so $56^{\\circ}$ is their included angle.\n\nApply the triangle area formula to those two sides and their included angle.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A&=\\frac12(CB)(CA)\\sin(\\angle BCA)\\\\\n&=\\frac12(10)(16)\\sin 56^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=80\\sin 56^{\\circ}\\\\\n&\\approx 66.32300580\\\\\n&\\approx 66.32.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area is $66.32$ square units. Keep full calculator precision until the final rounding."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719591 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c5d50fe-0ef2-509b-b1d9-b72794b82670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c5d50fe-0ef2-509b-b1d9-b72794b82670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719592} :answer-field/id #uuid "18764720-e3aa-5fa9-8509-71a4dd1a0f9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6216cd4b-1eaa-5609-902e-854d41124ecd" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7bc75c34b1669f67272f4c5f82a290d6a100704f8c2b1f4731fe12db606e6f97.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABC$, $CA=11$ and $CB=6$. The included angle is $\\angle ACB=104^{\\circ}$.\n\nRounded to **nearest tenth**, the area of $\\triangle ABC$ is {{field-1}} square units.\n\n> Use a scientific calculator in degree mode." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The sides $CA=11$ and $CB=6$ meet at $C$, so $104^{\\circ}$ is their included angle.\n\nApply the triangle area formula to those two sides and their included angle.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A&=\\frac12(CA)(CB)\\sin(\\angle ACB)\\\\\n&=\\frac12(11)(6)\\sin 104^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=33\\sin 104^{\\circ}\\\\\n&\\approx 32.01975897\\\\\n&\\approx 32.0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area is $32.0$ square units. Keep full calculator precision until the final rounding."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43eaa1da-964a-57c0-9995-5c05cc546989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43eaa1da-964a-57c0-9995-5c05cc546989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719589} :answer-field/id #uuid "495b6ac9-6991-588b-8061-b7af3791dccd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b4b5aa95-6a06-509c-b4b2-ab222474de7d" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8ef57b5ff247ada9b011c42923b0148fce2302b6f6a67f5a2a4d7e5ca53248b1.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABC$, $CB=17$ and $CA=8$. The included angle is $\\angle BCA=95^{\\circ}$.\n\nRounded to **nearest integer**, the area of $\\triangle ABC$ is {{field-1}} square units.\n\n> Use a scientific calculator in degree mode." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The sides $CB=17$ and $CA=8$ meet at $C$, so $95^{\\circ}$ is their included angle.\n\nApply the triangle area formula to those two sides and their included angle.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A&=\\frac12(CB)(CA)\\sin(\\angle BCA)\\\\\n&=\\frac12(17)(8)\\sin 95^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=68\\sin 95^{\\circ}\\\\\n&\\approx 67.74123947\\\\\n&\\approx 68.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area is $68$ square units. Keep full calculator precision until the final rounding."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad46c2b0-d099-5bab-bb3f-66da112405e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad46c2b0-d099-5bab-bb3f-66da112405e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719600} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8382bd5-c5e6-51d0-a5fa-15520403a8e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ea8c5c48-562a-54d2-8b7b-2d6fc655b116" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d11b09adf65955d5ff02adc7b54d2960fad9156a84bf0fda34c6954a41ebc315.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABC$, $BC=11$ and $BA=13$. The included angle is $\\angle CBA=90^{\\circ}$.\n\nRounded to **nearest integer**, the area of $\\triangle ABC$ is {{field-1}} square units.\n\n> Use a scientific calculator in degree mode." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The sides $BC=11$ and $BA=13$ meet at $B$, so $90^{\\circ}$ is their included angle.\n\nApply the triangle area formula to those two sides and their included angle.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal A&=\\frac12(BC)(BA)\\sin(\\angle CBA)\\\\\n&=\\frac12(11)(13)\\sin 90^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=71.5\\sin 90^{\\circ}\\\\\n&\\approx 71.50000000\\\\\n&\\approx 72.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area is $72$ square units. Keep full calculator precision until the final rounding."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58724fc4-c8a5-57e4-b946-2e2c267b00f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58724fc4-c8a5-57e4-b946-2e2c267b00f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719809} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4443099-6343-5da8-832a-bd7f8ac4c096" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "006228de-a027-5108-8173-b8d2cc090362" :question/problem "Find the area of convex quadrilateral $ABCD$, rounded to the **nearest tenth**. All lengths are in units.\n\n$DA=10$, $DC=9$, $DB=13$, $\\angle ADB=70^\\circ$, $\\angle BDC=25^\\circ$.\n\n![](images/20/2078f6e3479cfe8e9d176fb6008c4faa2c2a60dcb1fe3c800e7a002cdb9246a3.png)\n\nArea: {{field-1}} square units. Enter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point.\n\nA scientific calculator in degree mode may be used." :question/worked-solution "Diagonal $DB$ divides the quadrilateral into two nonoverlapping triangles.\n\n![](images/20/2078f6e3479cfe8e9d176fb6008c4faa2c2a60dcb1fe3c800e7a002cdb9246a3.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle DAB$, the sides of lengths $10$ and $13$ enclose the $70^\\circ$ angle. Applying the triangle area formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{DAB}&=\\frac12(10)(13)\\sin 70^\\circ\\\\\n&=65\\sin 70^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 61.0800.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $\\triangle DBC$, the sides of lengths $13$ and $9$ enclose the $25^\\circ$ angle. Applying the triangle area formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{DBC}&=\\frac12(13)(9)\\sin 25^\\circ\\\\\n&=58.5\\sin 25^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 24.7232.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two areas, retaining full calculator precision:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD}&=A_{DAB}+A_{DBC}\\\\\n&=65\\sin 70^\\circ+58.5\\sin 25^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 85.8032.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound only the final total: $\\boxed{85.8}$ square units."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c3fa5d4-f360-56a6-bcbe-e85626477450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c3fa5d4-f360-56a6-bcbe-e85626477450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719815} :answer-field/id #uuid "bebd45c4-14a8-5263-97a0-46cdf486a526" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "093f85c9-79f5-528e-bf35-f3f2b7886e15" :question/problem "Find the area of convex quadrilateral $ABCD$, rounded to the **nearest tenth**. All lengths are in units.\n\n$AB=9$, $AD=6$, $\\angle BAD=120^\\circ$, $BC=9$, $CD=15$, $\\angle BCD=60^\\circ$.\n\n![](images/e1/e1a0b34b59d2f6a3fe0242203cc5a83cdc620c8c3ddeec76a1e5bf5ce6b1412c.png)\n\nArea: {{field-1}} square units. Enter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point.\n\nA scientific calculator in degree mode may be used." :question/worked-solution "Diagonal $BD$ divides the quadrilateral into two nonoverlapping triangles.\n\n![](images/00/0064faca873ce4706f5b4cd612bb4b8f26ad0527229370fb08d41d1d9ef1f121.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABD$, the sides of lengths $9$ and $6$ enclose the $120^\\circ$ angle. Applying the triangle area formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABD}&=\\frac12(9)(6)\\sin 120^\\circ\\\\\n&=27\\sin 120^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 23.3827.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $\\triangle BCD$, the sides of lengths $9$ and $15$ enclose the $60^\\circ$ angle. Applying the triangle area formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{BCD}&=\\frac12(9)(15)\\sin 60^\\circ\\\\\n&=67.5\\sin 60^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 58.4567.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two areas, retaining full calculator precision:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD}&=A_{ABD}+A_{BCD}\\\\\n&=27\\sin 120^\\circ+67.5\\sin 60^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 81.8394.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound only the final total: $\\boxed{81.8}$ square units."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0a80e00-4dab-5645-a4cd-3e0064e10e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "106.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0a80e00-4dab-5645-a4cd-3e0064e10e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "106.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719817} :answer-field/id #uuid "54fbb47b-cf9c-5390-beb8-171e2b164a09" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "590fc041-a0bd-5c99-842a-9058a52d16b2" :question/problem "Find the area of parallelogram $ABCD$, rounded to the **nearest tenth**. All lengths are in units.\n\n$AB=13$, $AD=9$, $\\angle BAD=65^\\circ$.\n\n![](images/bb/bba7e1b0a80df6b27d62bb34fd49e3cc5237c91eecc80adfacefd6390da8064c.png)\n\nArea: {{field-1}} square units. Enter the rounded number using digits and a decimal point.\n\nA scientific calculator in degree mode may be used." :question/worked-solution "Diagonal $BD$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles.\n\n![](images/fb/fb8c290577729f96ae47a549413b77aa6bfd4d4df85d067a51e90a4aceff21d7.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABD$, the sides of lengths $13$ and $9$ enclose the $65^\\circ$ angle. Applying the triangle area formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABD}&=\\frac12(13)(9)\\sin 65^\\circ\\\\\n&=58.5\\sin 65^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 53.0190.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDouble the triangle area, retaining full calculator precision:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD}&=2A_{ABD}\\\\\n&=2\\left(58.5\\sin 65^\\circ\\right)\\\\\n&\\approx 106.0380.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound only the final total: $\\boxed{106.0}$ square units."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33cc6e9a-2823-5438-b11f-e74a0792783b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719806} {:answer/id #uuid "784a2941-1969-5d73-b48a-406ca7ee58f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "67.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719814} {:answer/id #uuid "e36c37fb-d08b-5995-9b2b-c5f121fb5894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "91.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719821} {:answer/id #uuid "ed829d20-1499-5949-813c-41517dfafc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "134.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719823} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c69665-a2f1-5f6a-ab1a-2f4ed71d7955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "784a2941-1969-5d73-b48a-406ca7ee58f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "67.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719814} :answer-field/id #uuid "75290814-6420-52a3-a758-427250b77276" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a94afa3b-3a8a-56cc-ae94-803cbb3b0a3d" :question/problem "Find the area of convex quadrilateral $ABCD$, rounded to the **nearest tenth**. All lengths are in units.\n\n$AB=6$, $AD=8$, $\\angle BAD=90^\\circ$, $BC=10$, $CD=10$, $\\angle BCD=60^\\circ$.\n\n![](images/ea/ea16d722bca35c459261b92c804c645064a95f33d7093ef989427e6a96a7d78b.png)\n\nA scientific calculator in degree mode may be used." :question/worked-solution "Diagonal $BD$ divides the quadrilateral into two nonoverlapping triangles.\n\n![](images/c5/c5fd00ab665309b62eee056be4805a0e9d035cdec734f3cd2789c21e8bec4ead.png)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABD$, the sides of lengths $6$ and $8$ enclose the $90^\\circ$ angle. Applying the triangle area formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABD}&=\\frac12(6)(8)\\sin 90^\\circ\\\\\n&=24\\sin 90^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 24.0000.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $\\triangle BCD$, the sides of lengths $10$ and $10$ enclose the $60^\\circ$ angle. Applying the triangle area formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{BCD}&=\\frac12(10)(10)\\sin 60^\\circ\\\\\n&=50\\sin 60^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 43.3013.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two areas, retaining full calculator precision:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD}&=A_{ABD}+A_{BCD}\\\\\n&=24\\sin 90^\\circ+50\\sin 60^\\circ\\\\\n&\\approx 67.3013.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound only the final total: $\\boxed{67.3}$ square units."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "323b0904-e434-5708-81ca-1d14bb301af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719805} {:answer/id #uuid "532ab908-3619-5fd4-ad13-16db857e8579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "94.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719807} {:answer/id #uuid "6f95ad23-72c9-5219-ab9b-934396ae7ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719811} {:answer/id #uuid "750d66a1-bada-53f0-9397-0a2ba36b3f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719812} {:answer/id #uuid "da038d29-1e8e-598f-8035-c7dd1e3aa184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719820}] :