ion until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $9\\,\\text{in}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6cc21be-1f63-5f98-93fb-6308436c3cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6cc21be-1f63-5f98-93fb-6308436c3cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725426} :answer-field/id #uuid "23da016f-7004-5388-a713-3af3f2e864ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "064a163c-f9e7-522d-9ee5-1e3bc6a8fd09" :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral CDAB with measurements](images/1e/1e20144abb107eeb5c452cecfad79159103871bcdd9e96cf3ec60ff461ece80d.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ is $3\\,\\text{cm}^{2}$. The sides $CD=4\\,\\text{cm}$ and $CB=7\\,\\text{cm}$ meet at $66^\\circ$. The area of $\\triangle DAB$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is {{field-1}} $\\text{cm}^{2}$.\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $CDB$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{CDB}&=\\frac12\\cdot CD\\cdot CB\\cdot\\sin\\angle DCB\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 4\\cdot 7\\cdot\\sin66^\\circ\\\\&\\approx12.789636\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ and the missing triangle $DAB$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{DAB}&=A_{CDB}-A_{CDAB}\\\\&=14\\sin66^\\circ-3\\\\&\\approx9.789636\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precisi