\&\\approx9.222721\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $9\\,\\text{in}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d44a2f-f04e-5c99-a882-2819dfa4df59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725349} {:answer/id #uuid "05047f70-163c-5d33-8e14-1af3560ef282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725350} {:answer/id #uuid "8810d092-a8ef-5ed2-a5d5-6d9533090966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725396} {:answer/id #uuid "d37153cc-f81a-5dcc-bda6-a0181bc0fa51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725410} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa3d01f-6bb9-5e78-be29-68465877bc3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02d44a2f-f04e-5c99-a882-2819dfa4df59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725349} :answer-field/id #uuid "86cc20da-0806-55c2-82da-72bac8afebc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d404bbfa-8dd0-5a2d-a8c0-c559d2ca2f19" :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral CDAB with measurements](images/bf/bf86dd66e68aa803862e9d743bff40c2c4e507b1504cd854e998c43b67babb59.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ is $6\\,\\text{in}^{2}$. The sides $CD=4.5\\,\\text{in}$ and $CB=9\\,\\text{in}$ meet at $110^\\circ$. What is the area of $\\triangle DAB$, rounded to the **nearest integer**?\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $CDB$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{CDB}&=\\frac12\\cdot CD\\cdot CB\\cdot\\sin\\angle DCB\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 4.5\\cdot 9\\cdot\\sin110^\\circ\\\\&\\approx19.028776\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ and the missing triangle $DAB$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{DAB}&=A_{CDB}-A_{CDAB}\\\\&=20.25\\sin110^\\circ-6\\\\&\\approx13.028776\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $13\\,\\text{in}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5412a8-fe6f-5cfd-be3f-5b9fda6f36cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725356} {:answer/id #uuid "268a3968-3426-5276-b2ec-4f7bb0fcc124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725366} {:answer/id #uuid "443f4b38-3e4b-597a-91b6-57381dcb62f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725373} {:answer/id #uuid "b95227d8-ce9a-57b4-a6f1-6b26cf45475d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725403} {:answer/id #uuid "df0f3b97-12fa-5577-b499-7e9137fb6fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f5412a8-fe6f-5cfd-be3f-5b9fda6f36cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725356} :answer-field/id #uuid "76736061-6aa1-5504-a874-53dc08d0a1df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e15248a8-3ab6-5f77-a9ff-9f9d66e09fb8" :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral BCDA with measurements](images/b0/b08362b6e0a41d7a1860dcb0e37152640d1262e9270714e8748b3f3ddc3081af.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $BCDA$ is $4\\,\\text{in}^{2}$. The sides $BC=7\\,\\text{in}$ and $BA=5\\,\\text{in}$ meet at $52^\\circ$. What is the area of $\\triangle CDA$, rounded to the **nearest integer**?\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $BCA$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{BCA}&=\\frac12\\cdot BC\\cdot BA\\cdot\\sin\\angle CBA\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 7\\cdot 5\\cdot\\sin52^\\circ\\\\&\\approx13.790188\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $BCDA$ and the missing triangle $CDA$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{CDA}&=A_{BCA}-A_{BCDA}\\\\&=17.5\\sin52^\\circ-4\\\\&\\approx9.790188\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $10\\,\\text{in}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145c2a76-ad68-5029-9196-465ab774db23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725359} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7f48e6-87b9-5f36-8cf8-dab22d3d8ea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725406} {:answer/id #uuid "d23aa305-7728-5819-bcfc-a697b199cb40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725408} {:answer/id #uuid "da2757da-98fa-5d30-8a6a-cca3eafd01a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725414} {:answer/id #uuid "dc161ed4-f0d0-53c7-8ef6-e3224493fe8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "145c2a76-ad68-5029-9196-465ab774db23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{in}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725359} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d255caa-37d3-5e91-a1b3-bb10ab76de51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e6cd0eda-9ad8-5a52-a131-166d8fbec899" :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral CDAB with measurements](images/40/40e1a732a1fa15bb08da6ed21d1df3da4d15b87cef3daf6bdcdd548aa2f303bf.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ is $6\\,\\text{in}^{2}$. The sides $CD=5\\,\\text{in}$ and $CB=9\\,\\text{in}$ meet at $42^\\circ$. What is the area of $\\triangle DAB$, rounded to the **nearest integer**?\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $CDB$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{CDB}&=\\frac12\\cdot CD\\cdot CB\\cdot\\sin\\angle DCB\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 5\\cdot 9\\cdot\\sin42^\\circ\\\\&\\approx15.055439\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $CDAB$ and the missing triangle $DAB$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{DAB}&=A_{CDB}-A_{CDAB}\\\\&=22.5\\sin42^\\circ-6\\\\&\\approx9.055439\\,\\text{in}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $9\\,\\text{in}^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2028ddcb-2790-5d04-b39a-1216b7f388e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725364} {:answer/id #uuid "27d85000-543e-5029-b503-47c7a82d0fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725367} {:answer/id #uuid "2942be53-e9b7-54e9-8211-244e09ff8232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725368} {:answer/id #uuid "94fc76f3-8b52-575b-b306-4e11d2585f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725398} {:answer/id #uuid "e45d4629-4dca-599a-870f-e4183f29c374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2942be53-e9b7-54e9-8211-244e09ff8232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{cm}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725368} :answer-field/id #uuid "878e4f79-a205-569f-b2a6-932536f767af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f014e895-4b1a-59d5-b6ba-886d028f55cb" :question/problem "![Concave quadrilateral DABC with measurements](images/85/859e1b1de8f994f597260f539c60411b175e652084a628e7e196d0236c1b31fe.png)\n\nThe area of the quadrilateral $DABC$ is $7\\,\\text{cm}^{2}$. The sides $DA=9\\,\\text{cm}$ and $DC=4\\,\\text{cm}$ meet at $70^\\circ$. What is the area of $\\triangle ABC$, rounded to the **nearest integer**?\n\nYou may use a scientific calculator." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First calculate the area of the enclosing triangle $DAC$. Use the two given sides and their included angle, with the calculator in degree mode.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{DAC}&=\\frac12\\cdot DA\\cdot DC\\cdot\\sin\\angle ADC\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot 9\\cdot 4\\cdot\\sin70^\\circ\\\\&\\approx16.914467\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe enclosing triangle consists of the quadrilateral $DABC$ and the missing triangle $ABC$. Subtract the quadrilateral area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A_{ABC}&=A_{DAC}-A_{DABC}\\\\&=18\\sin70^\\circ-7\\\\&\\approx9.914467\\,\\text{cm}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full precision until this subtraction is complete. Rounded to the nearest integer, the area is $10\\,\\text{cm}^{2}$."}]}
